# Workflow Diagram

## Overview
This folder contains the high-level workflow diagram for the QTC Workflow Queue (WFQ) Administrator Application.

The diagram explains how the software system operates at a high level, including:

- How the QTC Administrator connects to the application
- How HTTP requests and responses are handled
- How the WFQ Administrator Application communicates with the database
- How data is stored and retrieved from the Workflow Database
- What system components have access to workflow information

## Included Components
The workflow diagram includes the following major entities:

1. QTC Administrator (User)
2. WFQ Administrator Application
3. Workflow Database

## Data Flow
The workflow demonstrates:

- User requests sent through HTTP
- Application responses returned to the user
- Entity Framework Core / T-SQL database queries
- SQL results returned from the database

## Files
- `WorkflowDiagram.png` — Level 0 Data Flow Diagram (DFD)

## Purpose
The purpose of this diagram is to provide a visual representation of the system architecture and data flow for developers, testers, and project reviewers.
